# sgo.build — plan 0038's interp gate. The question WIRE-DIES-INTERP-TO-SGOLA
# has to answer before any of interp.go is ported: can a facade express the
# generated `appkit` surface, whose method signatures pass and return
# CGRect/CGPoint/CGSize BY VALUE? Every facade this repo has today binds an
# opaque handle or a scalar; a Go struct with fields, constructed on the Sgola
# side, is new.
#
# The bindings ride in as an ordinary godep (they are a plain Go module here),
# so nothing about this spike is about bindgen — only about the facade.
mode app
emitname interp-spike
binname interp-spike
gomod interpspike
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/appleptt ../go-pkgs/appleptt
